        question: "Why does HVAC equipment fail faster in the Florida Keys?",
        answer: "Constant salt air. Chloride deposits corrode condenser coils, electrical contacts, fasteners, and enclosures far faster than on the mainland, and the year-round humidity keeps surfaces wet enough for corrosion to proceed continuously. Standard inland equipment can fail in a few years. The engineering response is coastal-rated equipment with epoxy-coated coils and marine-grade enclosures, installed for drainage and rinsing, plus a maintenance plan with freshwater washdown schedules — the design assumes maintenance will happen and makes it easy.",
