        heading: "Power, Ventilation, Water, and Sanitation",
        body: "The MEP design for the shelter is a self-sufficiency package. The generator is sized from a shelter load list — lighting at shelter levels, ventilation fans, kitchen equipment, communications, device charging, and medical loads — with automatic transfer and fuel storage for the design duration plus margin. The fuel system is protected: above-flood, anchored tanks with containment, and a fueling plan that does not depend on post-storm deliveries. Critical panels and the transfer switch sit above the design flood elevation in a hardened electrical room.\n\nVentilation design handles the densest occupancy the building will ever see. The engineer sizes the shelter air handlers for the design population's fresh-air and cooling loads, with filtration appropriate for a crowded refuge and controls that switch the building to shelter mode. Potable water storage is calculated per person per day for the design duration, with distribution that works on generator power; the plumbing fixture count follows the shelter standard for the population, and the sanitary design includes backwater protection and, where feasible, on-site storage or treatment so the shelter's plumbing functions when the municipal sewer surcharges. The kitchen is designed to serve the shelter population from stored and delivered supplies, with refrigeration on emergency power.",
