        body: "The domestic water system is sized from a fixture-unit analysis of the real hotel: guest rooms, restaurants, banquet kitchens, spa, laundry, and irrigation, with diversity applied honestly so the booster pumps handle the morning peak without short-cycling at night. The engineer divides the tower into pressure zones — typically one per several floors — each with its own pressure-reducing or booster arrangement so the top floor sees a strong shower and the lower floors see safe pressures. Hot water recirculation is designed as a true engineered loop with balancing, because a 300-room hotel with dead-leg hot water wastes energy and breeds complaints in equal measure.\n\nCorrosion control is specified into every material. Copper or CPVC distribution, stainless or bronze valves, dielectric unions at every transition, and insulation that survives the humid mechanical spaces — the engineer writes the specification for the salt air that infiltrates every coastal mechanical room. Water treatment is designed for the local supply chemistry: softening or conditioning where hardness scales fixtures and water heaters, and the treatment equipment itself sits above the design flood elevation with bypass valving so the hotel keeps water during maintenance.",
