        heading: "Gulf Coast Daycare Flood Design Checklist",
        body: "Use this checklist before the floor plan is finalized:\n\n• Finished floor at or above the design flood elevation plus freeboard; beyond-minimum elevation evaluated\n• All critical MEP above the flood line; below-floor enclosures flood-tolerant or breakaway\n• Impact-rated glazing and protected openings throughout the wind-borne debris region\n• Roof edge, flashing, and wall-to-roof connections verified for the design wind speed\n• Emergency power for lighting, communications, refrigeration, and cooling with realistic fuel duration\n• Evacuation route graded to stay passable; pickup loop on high ground clear of flood paths\n• Backwater valves on sanitary; interior materials selected to dry rather than require demolition\n• State childcare licensing facility standards and local emergency-response times confirmed",
